==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/lɛs/}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-less.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-less.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛs|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Adverb from {{inh|en|enm|les|id=less}}, {{m|enm|lesse|id=less}}, {{m|enm|leasse}}, {{m|enm|lasse|id=less}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lǣs|t=smaller, less}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*laisiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leys-|t=to shrink, grow thin, be gentle}}.{{rfv-etym|en}} Cognate with {{cog|ofs|lēs|t=less}}, {{cog|osx|lēs|t=less}}. According to Kroonen (2013), from a northern Indo-European root {{der|en|ine-pro|*leh₂is-}} or ''*leh₃is-'', which he connects to {{cog|lt|liesas|t=lean}}.

Determiner and preposition from {{inh|en|enm|lees}}, {{m|enm|lesse}}, {{m|enm|leasse}}, {{m|enm|lasse}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lǣssa|t=less}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*laisizan-}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*laisiz|t=smaller, lesser, fewer, lower}} (see above). Cognate with {{cog|ofs|lessa|t=less}}.

Verb from {{inh|en|enm|lessen}}, from the determiner.

Noun from {{inh|en|enm|lesse}}, from the determiner.

====Adverb====
{{en-adverb|-}}

# To a smaller extent or degree. 
#: {{ux|en|The supposed benefit is actually '''less''' a benefit and more a drawback.}}
## {{n-g|Functioning as a comparative of '''''[[little]]'''}}.
##: {{ux|en|I slept little [[last night]], but even '''less''' the night before.}}
## {{n-g|Used for constructing syntactic diminutive comparatives of adjectives and adverbs.}}
##: {{ux|en|This gadget is '''less''' useful than I expected.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'm not any '''less''' happy for being on my own.}}
##: {{ux|en|Please do your work a little '''less''' hurriedly.}}
##* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=I corralled the judge, and we started off across the fields, in no very mild state of fear of that gentleman's wife, whose vigilance was seldom relaxed. And thus we came by a circuitous route to Mohair, the judge occupied by his own guilty thoughts, and I by others not '''less''' disturbing.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|author=Lester Del Rey|title=Rockets Through Space: The Story of Man's Preparations to Explore the Universe
|passage=This section of space is much '''less''' empty than that between the stars, {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=November 7, 2012|author=Matt Bai|title=Winning a Second Term, Obama Will Confront Familiar Headwinds|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0
|passage=That brief moment after the election four years ago, when many Americans thought Mr. Obama’s election would presage a new, '''less''' fractious political era, now seems very much a thing of the past.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251106105818/https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/07/us/politics/in-president-obamas-second-term-familiar-challenges.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0|archivedate=6 November 2025}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katrina-g-claw Katrina G. Claw]
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/rapid-evolution-in-eggs-and-sperm Rapid Evolution in Eggs and Sperm]
|volume=101|issue=3|magazine=w:American Scientist
|passage=In plants, the ability to recognize self from nonself plays an important role in fertilization, because self-fertilization will result in '''less''' diverse offspring than fertilization with pollen from another individual.}}

