====Determiner====
{{en-head|det}}

# A smaller amount of; not as much; {{en-comparative of|little}}. {{defdate|from 12th c.}}
#: {{ant|en|more}}
#: {{ux|en|I prefer it with '''less''' sugar.}}
#: {{ux|en|I have '''less''' tea than coffee.}}
#: {{ux|en|There is (even) '''less''' water left now.}}<!--parallel to the usex at ''little''--> 
#: {{ux|en|You have even '''less''' sense than an inanimate object.}}
# {{lb|en|proscribed}} [[fewer|Fewer]]; a smaller number of. {{defdate|from 9th c. at latest}}
#: {{ux|en|There are '''less''' people here now.}}
#: {{ux|en|Now there are three '''less''' green bottles hanging on the wall.}}
#: {{ux|en|The express checkout lane is for those with ten items or '''less''', and I have '''less''' than ten items.}}
#: {{ux|en|I saw '''less''' than a dozen people.}}<!-- Dictionary.com says this is an adjective 'less', but some other authorities and this Wiktionary entry appear to consider this kind of 'less' to be a determiner -->
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1579|author=Lyly|title=Euphues|page=208
|passage=I thinke there are few Vniuersities that haue '''lesse''' faultes than Oxford, many that haue more.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1681|author=John Houghton|title=A Collection For the Improvement of Husbandry and Trade|page=263
|passage=... on his land he will have less manure, less corn, and '''less''' people; ...}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Thomas M Pryor|journal=New York Times|date=7 Sep 1952
|passage=This is not a happy situation as far as the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employes is concerned because it means '''less''' jobs for the union's members here at home.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=w:George R.R. Martin|title=A Clash of Kings|page=555|publisher=Bantam|year_published=2011
|passage=No '''less''' than four standard-bearers went before them, carrying huge crimson banners emblazoned with the golden lion.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Timandra Harkness|journal=The Guardian|date=16 Dec 2003
|passage=Although my hosts, G S Aviation, can teach you to fly in Wiltshire, an intensive week at their French airfield means '''less''' problems with the weather, cheap but good living, and complete removal from any distractions.}}

