====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[smaller|Smaller]] in size, extent, degree, importance, worth, etc.
#: {{ant|en|greater}}<!--in some cases, although in some it would be awkward-->
#: {{ux|en|All my cares grew '''less''' until completely gone.}}
#: {{ux|en|Three is '''less''' than four.}}
#: {{ux|en|24 is sort-of like 25, but '''less'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|No '''less''' a person than the queen replied.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1624|author=John Smith|title=Generall Historie|publisher=Kupperman|year_published=1988|page=141
|passage=Those Rattels are somewhat like the chape of a Rapier, but '''lesse''', which they take from the taile of a snake.}}
#*: {{...}} by how much the Regent went every day '''less''' in her authority, so much more did the audacity of the Confederates, and the rest who held Intelligence with them, increase: {{...}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1711|journal=The Spectator|issue=126
|passage=We are likewise ready to maintain with the hazard of all that is near and dear to us, that six is '''less''' than seven in all times and all places {{...}}.}}
#*: For many a petty king ere Arthur came / Ruled in this isle, and ever waging war / Each upon the other, wasted all the land; {{...}} / And so there grew great tracts of wilderness, / Wherein the beast was ever more and more, / But man was '''less''' and '''less''', till Arthur came. 
#* {{rfdate|en}}, Halifax, quoted in '''1878''', ''Poetical Quotations from Chaucer to Tennyson'', page 398:
#*: 'Tis '''less''' to conquer, than to make wars cease, / And, without fighting, awe the world to peace.
## {{n-g|Used attributively, where {{m|en|lesser}} would now be used instead.}}
##* {{RQ:Thoreau Walden|chapter=Economy|passage=Such too, to a greater or '''less''' extent, is the condition of the operatives of every denomination in England, which is the great workhouse of the world.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1885|author=Edward James Reed|title=A Treatise on the Stability of Ships|passage=It is also easy to see that the straight line, representing the locus of centres of buoyancy for a rectangular section, must lie at a '''less''' inclination to the base (i.e., to the horizontal) than a line representing the locus of such centres for a parabolic section {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1886|author=Robert Louis Stevenson|title=Kidnapped
|passage=This he said, thinking that Alan would be pleased; but the Highlandman’s vanity was ready to startle at a '''less''' matter than that.}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# A [[smaller]] amount or quantity.
#: {{ux|en|'''Less''' is better, because [[less is more|'''less''' is more]].}}
#: {{ux|en|I have '''less''' to do today than yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|en|Last month '''less''' of my salary was [[taken up]] with household expenses, but I still want to pay '''less''' in taxes.}}
#: {{ux|en|I think there's '''less''' of a problem in that regard.}}
# Something of lower importance or severity.

